-- module `alias_main` — #965(a): `walkFieldAccess` files an alias-qualified
-- `D.aliasBar` reference at the ENCLOSING decl's `curLoc`.  Here the enclosing
-- decl is a wrapper spelled `aliasBar` TOO, so that span really does spell the
-- old name and F3(d) span verification waves it through — the emitted edit
-- rewrote THIS module's own definition head and never touched `D.aliasBar`,
-- leaving `Unbound variable: D.aliasBar`.  It corrupts an unrelated binder's
-- definition, which is exactly what F3(d) exists to prevent.
-- ⚠️ THE LINE NUMBERS BELOW ARE THE TRANSCRIPT'S CLICK COORDINATES — keep this
-- header exactly 9 lines.
import alias_lib as D

export aliasBar : Int -> Int
aliasBar n = D.aliasBar n

export aliasUse : Int
aliasUse = aliasBar 1
